                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a188fd36-9449-3e6e-9a8c-fdde70fef89d",
                        "entry_id": "25422a8c-eb5a-3ee0-b73b-f7934068dceb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To poke in an exploratory manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0eaf55f8-5bbe-4d6d-a464-426570703465",
                                "sense_id": "a188fd36-9449-3e6e-9a8c-fdde70fef89d",
                                "text": "I dare say, Mr Wauverley, ye never kend that a' the eggs that were sae weel roasted at supper in the Ha'-house were aye turned by our Davie; — there's no the like o' him ony gate for powtering wi' his fingers amang the het peat-ashes, and roasting eggs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30cc6c43-912a-45b5-a6f7-75afa5647baf",
                                "sense_id": "a188fd36-9449-3e6e-9a8c-fdde70fef89d",
                                "text": "Having worked and powtered away for a minute or two, the operator suddenly dropped the outlandish instrument, and uplifting his two hands, like the minister when pronouncing the dismissal, he exclaimed, \" My stars and garters, what a mighty development!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "545503dc-b84b-4285-afde-7523b3f55994",
                                "sense_id": "a188fd36-9449-3e6e-9a8c-fdde70fef89d",
                                "text": "So we got nowhere in particular ; but learnt a good deal, having ' powtered up and down a bit and had a rattling day.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1b31580-a7de-4324-805c-8812ee66c17d",
                                "sense_id": "a188fd36-9449-3e6e-9a8c-fdde70fef89d",
                                "text": "He had seen pigs like Christy powtering in the slops, all grunt and hair."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
